## Modeling Calendar Events

A calendar event has a date and a type. The type determines what extra information (if any) the event carries.

### The Date Struct

```xiom
type Date = {
  day: Int;
  month: Int;
  year: Int;
}
```

### The EventType Enum

```xiom
enum EventType {
  Meeting,
  Birthday,
  Holiday(name: Str),
  Deadline,
}
```

### The Event Struct

```xiom
type Event = {
  date: Date;
  kind: EventType;
}
```

### Creating Events

```xiom
let christmas = Event{
  date: Date{ day: 25; month: 12; year: 2026; };
  kind: EventType.Holiday("Christmas");
};

let deadline = Event{
  date: Date{ day: 15; month: 7; year: 2026; };
  kind: EventType.Deadline;
};
```

### Formatting an Event

```xiom
fn format(e: Event) -> Str {
  let date_str = e.date.day + "/" + e.date.month + "/" + e.date.year;
  match e.kind {
    Meeting => { return "Meeting on " + date_str; }
    Birthday => { return "Birthday on " + date_str; }
    Holiday(name) => { return name + " on " + date_str; }
    Deadline => { return "Deadline on " + date_str; }
  }
}
```

### Using It

```xiom
format(christmas);  // "Christmas on 25/12/2026"
format(deadline);   // "Deadline on 15/7/2026"
```

